From de60f8cd1d1d82b1ac9efe5a91e6358f0c0087f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 05:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] EXA: choose the 2D engine mode for solid fills by bits
 per pixel

Broken: viaExaPrepareSolid_H2/_H6 passed the pixmap's depth to
viaAccelSetMode(), which only knows bits per pixel (8, 16, 32). Depth 24,
the screen and every window-format pixmap, matched nothing, so every
solid fill on them was done in software. Under MigrationHeuristic
"always" each such fill also copied the destination out of video memory
and back, so a full-screen background fill cost tens of milliseconds and
the next composite waited for the upload.

Found: VIA_TRACE logging of PrepareSolid failures and EXA transfers while
neomaster drew: two failed PrepareSolid calls at the start of every frame,
each followed by a download of the back buffer.

Fix: pass bitsPerPixel, as PrepareCopy already does.
---
 src/via_exa_h2.c | 2 +-
 src/via_exa_h6.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/via_exa_h2.c b/src/via_exa_h2.c
index c1056a7..982fad3 100644
--- a/src/via_exa_h2.c
+++ b/src/via_exa_h2.c
@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@ viaExaPrepareSolid_H2(PixmapPtr pPixmap, int alu, Pixel planeMask, Pixel fg)
     if (exaGetPixmapPitch(pPixmap) & 7)
         return FALSE;
 
-    if (!viaAccelSetMode(pPixmap->drawable.depth, tdc))
+    if (!viaAccelSetMode(pPixmap->drawable.bitsPerPixel, tdc))
         return FALSE;
 
     if (!viaAccelPlaneMaskHelper_H2(tdc, planeMask))
diff --git a/src/via_exa_h6.c b/src/via_exa_h6.c
index 136e6e0..4cb62cd 100644
--- a/src/via_exa_h6.c
+++ b/src/via_exa_h6.c
@@ -174,7 +174,7 @@ viaExaPrepareSolid_H6(PixmapPtr pPixmap, int alu, Pixel planeMask, Pixel fg)
     if (exaGetPixmapPitch(pPixmap) & 7)
         return FALSE;
 
-    if (!viaAccelSetMode(pPixmap->drawable.depth, tdc))
+    if (!viaAccelSetMode(pPixmap->drawable.bitsPerPixel, tdc))
         return FALSE;
 
     if (!viaAccelPlaneMaskHelper_H6(tdc, planeMask))
-- 
